		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=28900#p28900"><![CDATA[
hello. i'd like to announce to the bullet community that Cycling 74's Max 6 interactive media software incorporates the Bullet physics engine for our jit.phys objects.<br><br>Max is a graphical programming environment that is used to create media rich interactive software for various applications.<br>you can find out more about Max here:<br><a href="http://cycling74.com/whatismax/" class="postlink">http://cycling74.com/whatismax/</a><br><a href="http://cycling74.com/products/max/" class="postlink">http://cycling74.com/products/max/</a><br><br>here is an introductory video that covers Max basics:<br><a href="http://cycling74.com/videos/" class="postlink">http://cycling74.com/videos/</a><br><br>we just wrapped up a two week spotlight on our physics objects, so we have lots of new material documenting their use here:<br><a href="http://cycling74.com/physics/" class="postlink">http://cycling74.com/physics/</a><br><br>and finally, here is some eye candy showing many of the physics features in Max.<br><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RjgJKsVBqbw" class="postlink">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RjgJKsVBqbw</a><br><br>if you are looking for a software that gives your realtime interactive control of a physics scene, allowing you to quickly prototype and test out new ideas, Max might be for you.  the software is available as a fully functional 30 day demo, so please give it a look.<br><a href="http://cycling74.com/downloads/" class="postlink">http://cycling74.com/downloads/</a><br><br>thanks for reading, and don't hesitate to reply here with any questions.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2364">robtherich</a> — Tue Oct 02, 2012 9:36 pm</p><hr />
